@startuml 02-browse-flow
skinparam backgroundColor White
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Sans
skinparam roundCorner 6
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFFF0
skinparam NoteBorderColor #999999
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F4F8
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #555555
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #F4F4F8
skinparam ClassBorderColor #555555
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #F4F4F8
skinparam StateBorderColor #555555
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #F4F4F8
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #555555
title Browse flow\nview movies -> select movie -> select theater -> view seats

actor "End user" as User
participant "HTTP client" as Client
box "moviebackend process" #F8F8F8
    participant "PublicController" as Controller
    participant "BookingService" as Service
    participant "Catalog" as Catalog
end box

== Step 1: view all playing movies ==
User -> Client : open the app
Client -> Controller : GET /api/v1/movies
Controller -> Service : listPlayingMovies()
Service -> Catalog : listPlayingMovies()
activate Catalog
note right of Catalog
  lock -> collect the movie ids that
  appear in m_showtimes -> copy those
  movies out -> unlock.
  A movie with no screening is not
  "playing" and is not listed.
end note
Catalog --> Service : vector<Movie>
deactivate Catalog
Service --> Controller : vector<Movie>
Controller --> Client : 200 [ {id:"m1", title:"The Silent Protocol", ...}, ... ]
Client --> User : show the list

== Step 2: select a movie ==
User -> Client : tap "The Silent Protocol"
Client -> Controller : GET /api/v1/movies/m1
Controller -> Service : getMovie("m1")
Service -> Catalog : getMovie("m1")
Catalog --> Service : Movie (a **copy** - never a reference into locked state)
Service --> Controller : Movie
Controller --> Client : 200 { id:"m1", duration_minutes:110, ... }

== Step 3: see all theaters showing that movie ==
Client -> Controller : GET /api/v1/movies/m1/theaters
Controller -> Service : listTheatersShowingMovie("m1")
Service -> Catalog : listTheatersShowingMovie("m1")
activate Catalog
Catalog -> Catalog : requireMovieLocked("m1")
note right of Catalog
  An unknown movie is a **404**, not an
  empty list - the client must be able
  to tell "no such film" from
  "not on anywhere".
end note
Catalog --> Service : vector<Theater>
deactivate Catalog
Controller --> Client : 200 [ {id:"t1", name:"Cinema Central", seat_capacity:20}, ... ]
Client --> User : show the theaters

== Step 4: select a theater, see the timeline ==
User -> Client : tap "Cinema Central"
Client -> Controller : GET /api/v1/movies/m1/theaters/t1/showtimes
Controller -> Service : listShowtimes("m1","t1")
activate Service
Service -> Catalog : listShowtimes("m1","t1")
Catalog --> Service : vector<Showtime> (ordered by start time)
loop for each showtime
    Service -> Catalog : listAvailableSeats(showtimeId)
    Catalog --> Service : free seat labels
end
note right of Service
  One short lock acquisition per
  showtime rather than one long one.
  The counts are advisory anyway, so a
  perfectly consistent view across all
  showtimes would buy nothing and would
  lengthen the section bookings compete for.
end note
Service --> Controller : vector<ShowtimeAvailability>
deactivate Service
Controller --> Client : 200 [ {id:"s1", start_time:"09:00", available_seats:20}, ... ]
Client --> User : show times, greying out sold-out ones

== Step 5: see available seats ==
User -> Client : tap the 09:00 screening
Client -> Controller : GET /api/v1/showtimes/s1/seats
Controller -> Service : getShowtime("s1")
Controller -> Service : listAvailableSeats("s1")
Controller -> Service : listBookedSeats("s1")
Controller --> Client : 200 {\n  available_seats:["a1","a2","a3",...],\n  booked_seats:[],\n  seat_capacity:20 }
Client --> User : render the seat map

note over User, Catalog #FFF8E0
  These counts are a **snapshot**. A seat shown as free here
  can be taken by somebody else a microsecond later - which is
  exactly why the booking call re-checks under the lock rather
  than trusting what the client was shown.
end note

@enduml
